      "id": "white",
      "name": "Pavonem",
      "description": "Peacock eyes, and built the way one is: a small dark pupil, a ring of the horse's own coat around it left completely alone, and a broad outer leaf around that - each zone about a fifth, a half and the whole of the width, and every one of them a little taller than it is wide. The ring is the part that makes it read: paint the middle and it stops being an eye and becomes a spot. The leaf is the same colour as the pupil but much weaker, so the three zones go strong, bare, faint from the centre out. It is never alone - ordinary small spots always ring the eyes - and it works on any base, stacking happily with tobiano and the rest.",
